+### Wasmer
+
+[Wasmer](https://wasmer.io/) builds Dashy from Git and serves the generated `dist` folder as static files (`yarn install`, then `yarn run build`). The button opens Wasmer's import page for this public repository, where you review the configuration and click Deploy; it does not create a copy of the repository in your GitHub account. To use your own `user-data/conf.yml`, fork the repo and import your fork instead. There are no rewrite rules on this host, so open Dashy from its root URL: reloading a sub-route such as `/workspace` or `/minimal` returns a 404. Status checks, the CORS proxy and saving config through the UI need Dashy's Node server, so they don't work here.
+
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-171717?logo=wasmer&logoColor=white)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=lissy93%2Fdashy)
+
+
 ### Cloudflare Pages
 
 [Cloudflare Pages](https://pages.cloudflare.com/) is static hosting on Cloudflare's edge. Import the repo, set build command `yarn build`, and set output directory `dist`.
